                <head>437. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On November 10, 1970, Prime Minister Suleyman Demirel postponed his visit to the
                    United States, citing among other reasons his desire to be in Ankara when the
                    Turkish Parliament voted on an opium licensing bill.</p>
            </div>
